  "exec_summary": "The European Securities and Markets Authority has launched a consultation on guidelines for a shortened settlement cycle of T+1, which is a significant development in EU regulatory framework. In Belgium, there are no notable regulatory developments this week. Meanwhile, the European Central Bank has observed that cash remains the most widely accepted payment method in the euro area, which may have implications for payment institutions and fintech firms operating in the region, such as those licensed by BaFin under the E-Money and Payment Institution License. The ESMA consultation on T+1 guidelines is the most significant regulatory development this week, with potential impact on market participants and post-trade processes.",
